    "notes": "1. 'Total revenues and other income' is mapped to 'total_revenue' and is the sum of its three listed components. 2. 'Total costs and other deductions' includes 'Other taxes and duties' and 'Interest expense', which are not part of standard operating costs. Therefore, 'total_operating_cost' is constructed from all other cost line items under 'Costs and other deductions' except for 'Interest expense' and 'Other taxes and duties'. 3. 'Other taxes and duties' are considered non-income taxes (e.g., property, excise, severance) and are part of operating costs. They are already included in 'Production and manufacturing expenses' and 'Selling, general and administrative expenses' per Note 19, so they are not listed separately to avoid double-counting. 4. 'Net income' is mapped to 'Net income (loss) attributable to ExxonMobil'. 5. 'Taxes' is mapped to 'Income tax expense (benefit)'. 6. 'Interest expense' is mapped directly to 'interest_expenses'. 7. All values are taken directly from the primary income statement. Supplementary tables provide detail but do not change the totals used.",
